# Searchable directory: every calculator stays available without JavaScript.
home=f'''<div class="wrap"><section class="hero"><div><span class="pill">A little clarity for your next big goal</span><h1>Know your grade.<br><em>Plan your next move.</em></h1><p class="lead">Less guessing. More confidence. Work out what you need on your final, understand your average, and make a plan.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href="/final-grade-calculator/">Plan my final grade <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="#calculators">Explore all tools</a></div><div class="checks"><span>Always free</span><span>No account needed</span><span>Clear formulas</span></div></div>{calculator('final',True)}</section><section class="section" id="calculators"><div class="section-title"><div><span class="eyebrow">The student toolkit</span><h2>One less thing to work out.</h2></div><p>Choose the tool that fits your question.</p></div><div class="tool-filters"><label class="field">Search 30 free tools<input type="search" id="tool-search" placeholder="Try GPA, attendance or final exam"></label><label class="field">Category<select id="tool-category"><option value="all">All tools</option><option value="grades">Grades &amp; targets</option><option value="scores">Tests &amp; scores</option><option value="gpa">GPA planning</option><option value="study">Study planning</option></select></label></div><p id="tool-count" role="status">30 tools available</p><div class="grid" id="tool-directory">{cards(tools)}</div></section></div><section class="band"><div class="wrap band-grid"><div><h3>Understand the answer</h3><p>Formulas and worked examples make every result easier to check.</p></div><div><h3>Your grades stay with you</h3><p>Calculations run in your browser. No accounts or uploaded transcripts.</p></div><div><h3>Built for real course rules</h3><p>Clear assumptions help you choose the right method for your syllabus.</p></div></div></section><div class="wrap"><section class="section"><div class="section-title"><div><span class="eyebrow">Beyond the number</span><h2>Make sense of your grades.</h2></div>{link('guides','All study guides →')}</div><div class="grid">{''.join(f'<a class="card" href="/{s}/"><span class="eyebrow">Grade guide</span><h3>{t}</h3><p>{d}</p><span class="arrow">Read the guide →</span></a>' for s,t,d in [('guides/weighted-vs-points-grades','Weighted grades vs. total points','Why two sensible calculations can produce different answers.'),('guides/what-grade-do-i-need-to-pass','What grade do I need to pass?','Turn your actual passing threshold into a practical exam target.'),('guides/gpa-scales-us-uk-canada','Grading across the US, UK & Canada','Why a universal percentage-to-GPA conversion can mislead.')])}</div></section></div>'''
