article('about','About GradeTargetCalc','Practical tools that make academic planning easier.',f'''<h2>Our purpose</h2><p>GradeTargetCalc is an independent educational calculator project. It helps students estimate grades, understand common formulas and compare academic targets without creating an account.</p><h2>How we build the tools</h2><p>We make the assumptions visible, explain the mathematics and include worked examples. Calculations run locally in your browser. We do not request transcripts or claim access to a school’s records.</p><h2>Content and editorial process</h2><p>We use AI-assisted tools for drafting and development. Published learning guides explain the implemented formulas with reproducible examples and tool-specific limitations. Formula and input checks help us identify errors; they do not constitute review by your institution or an independent academic certification.</p><h2>Scope and independence</h2><p>We are not a university, examination board or academic advising service. We are not affiliated with the institutions cited in our guides. Estimates cannot replace an institution’s official results or regulations.</p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>We aim to correct errors and clarify unclear assumptions. See our {link('methodology','methodology')} and {link('contact','contact page')} for reporting information.</p>''')
contact_content=f'<p>For calculation errors, accessibility issues or privacy requests, email <a href="mailto:{esc(CONTACT)}">{esc(CONTACT)}</a>.</p>' if CONTACT else '<div class="status">Preview notice: a public contact address is awaiting owner verification. This page is not ready for public launch.</div>'
article('contact','Contact us','Help improve a calculation or report a problem.',contact_content+'''<h2>Reporting a calculation issue</h2><p>Include the calculator name, non-sensitive example inputs, the result you expected and the result shown. If possible, explain the formula or syllabus rule involved. For a display problem, include your device and browser name.</p><h2>Protect your privacy</h2><p>Please do not send student IDs, transcripts, passwords or other private records. We cannot access or amend official academic results. Your institution is the right contact for grading decisions.</p>''')
article('methodology','Calculation methodology','Transparent assumptions, reproducible examples and clear limits.',f'''<h2>How results are calculated</h2><p>Our tools use the formulas shown on each calculator page. Grade and score inputs normally range from 0 to 100. GPA inputs use numeric institution-defined points and the selected maximum scale. Blank, non-finite and out-of-range values are rejected.</p><h2>Precision</h2><p>Calculations use JavaScript floating-point numbers. Ordinary results display rounded to two decimal places. Required final scores round upward to two decimals to avoid understating a minimum. Official systems may use different rounding or truncation rules.</p><h2>Validation and review</h2><p>Development checks cover worked examples, boundary values, invalid inputs and the consistency of weighted averages. These checks are not independent academic certification. Contact us with a reproducible issue if a result appears incorrect.</p><h2>What is not modeled</h2><p>Some dedicated tools let you model a selected retake policy, equally weighted dropped scores or a stated must-pass threshold. These rules are never inferred from a school name. Other calculators do not apply them automatically. Curved or standardized scores, extra credit and official degree classifications are not modeled. Read the calculator-specific assumptions and your syllabus.</p><h2>Reference methods</h2><ul><li><a href="https://www.registrar.illinois.edu/courses-grades/calculate-your-gpa/">University of Illinois: credit-weighted GPA</a></li><li><a href="https://students.ok.ubc.ca/academic-success/grades-performance/">UBC: grading and GPA conversions</a></li><li><a href="https://www.manchester.ac.uk/study/international/study-abroad-exchange/support/grading-assessment/">Manchester: grading and assessment</a></li></ul><p>{link('contact','Report an issue')}</p>''')
article('privacy-policy','Privacy policy','What this version of GradeTargetCalc does with your information.',f'''<p>Effective date: 1 November 2026. This policy describes the current version and will be updated before new data services are enabled.</p><h2>Calculator inputs</h2><p>Your grades and calculator inputs are processed in your browser. This version does not send them to us, store them on a server or put them in page URLs. Inputs reset when you reload or leave the page.</p><h2>Theme preference</h2><p>If you select a light or dark theme, the site stores that preference in your browser’s local storage. You can remove it by clearing site data in your browser. Grade inputs are not saved in local storage.</p><h2>Hosting and technical information</h2><p>Your hosting provider receives information needed to deliver web pages, such as your IP address, requested URL and browser information. This site is hosted on GitHub Pages; its <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">privacy statement</a> describes its processing.</p><h2>Analytics, advertising and cookies</h2><p>This version does not load Google Analytics, Google AdSense or third-party advertising scripts. It does not set advertising or analytics cookies. If these services are added, this policy and the site’s consent choices must be updated before activation. No advertising consent is collected in this version because advertising is not enabled.</p><h2>Messages and privacy requests</h2><p>If you contact us by email, the email provider processes your message and sender information. We use messages to respond and investigate issues; please avoid sensitive academic records. Email <a href="mailto:{esc(CONTACT)}">{esc(CONTACT)}</a> for privacy questions, requests about messages you have sent, or correction reports.</p><h2>Children and academic records</h2><p>The tools do not require an account, age, name or student identifier. Do not submit children’s personal information or academic records through correspondence. External websites linked from this site have their own privacy practices.</p>''')
article('terms','Terms and conditions','Please use the tools as planning estimates.',f'''<p>Effective date: 1 November 2026.</p><h2>Use of the tools</h2><p>GradeTargetCalc provides free educational calculations and explanations. You may use the tools for personal or classroom planning. Do not use the site to disrupt service or misrepresent estimates as official academic records.</p><h2>Accuracy and academic decisions</h2><p>Results depend on your inputs and the assumptions shown. We aim for accurate mathematics, but cannot guarantee that a result matches your institution’s rules. Confirm requirements with your instructor or registrar before making academic decisions.</p><h2>Availability and changes</h2><p>Tools and content may change or be unavailable. We may correct errors and update these terms. Material changes will be reflected in the effective date.</p><h2>Responsibility</h2><p>To the extent permitted by applicable law, the site is provided as available without warranties of uninterrupted operation or suitability for a particular academic outcome. Nothing in these terms excludes rights or responsibilities that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p><h2>Original content and external references</h2><p>Site branding, text and implementation belong to their respective rights holders. External references are provided for context and do not imply endorsement. Contact us through the {link('contact','contact page')} about corrections or rights concerns.</p>''')
